WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.606 --> 00:00:06.293
- [Coss] Yo BuzzFeed,
my name is Coss Marte

00:00:06.293 --> 00:00:08.391
and my personal transformation happened

00:00:08.391 --> 00:00:10.407
in a nine by six prison cell.

00:00:10.407 --> 00:00:13.157
(dramatic music)

00:00:14.725 --> 00:00:17.065
I was raised in a heavily
drug infested community

00:00:17.065 --> 00:00:19.452
in the lower east side
section of Manhattan.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.016
People would ask me
"what do you want to be

00:00:21.016 --> 00:00:22.378
"when you grow up?"

00:00:22.378 --> 00:00:25.311
I'd tell em that I wanted to be rich

00:00:25.311 --> 00:00:26.584
and the first opportunity I got

00:00:26.584 --> 00:00:29.429
was through the world of drugs.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.282
I started smoking at the age of 11

00:00:31.282 --> 00:00:33.955
and at the age of 13 I made my first sale.

00:00:33.955 --> 00:00:36.549
This led me to the corner
on Broom and Elder street,

00:00:36.549 --> 00:00:38.071
where I began to pitch all the drugs

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.494
with the local guys who
respected my hustle.

00:00:40.494 --> 00:00:42.387
By the age of 19, I was the leader

00:00:42.387 --> 00:00:45.638
of a cocaine distributing
ring in New York City.

00:00:45.638 --> 00:00:47.938
I was making over two
million dollars a year.

00:00:47.938 --> 00:00:51.760
My first run with NYPD was at
the age of 13, and from then,

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.602
I was in and out of jail
for the next few years.

00:00:54.602 --> 00:00:57.354
When I was 23, I was
caught by federal agents

00:00:57.354 --> 00:01:00.269
and was sentenced to
seven years in prison.

00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:01.950
During my incarceration

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:05.799
I was overweight and extremely unhealthy.

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.076
The doctors in prison told me

00:01:07.076 --> 00:01:09.886
that I could die of a heart
attack within five years.

00:01:09.886 --> 00:01:12.513
But with a seven year
sentence in front of me,

00:01:12.513 --> 00:01:13.671
I was determined.

00:01:13.671 --> 00:01:16.252
I was not going to die in prison.

00:01:16.252 --> 00:01:17.857
So I started working out.

00:01:17.857 --> 00:01:21.229
I developed a workout routine
using just my body weight

00:01:21.229 --> 00:01:23.857
that could be done in a small prison cell.

00:01:23.857 --> 00:01:26.950
And, in just six months, I lost 70 pounds.

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:29.092
Then I started training other inmates

00:01:29.092 --> 00:01:30.785
and I helped 20 inmates lose

00:01:30.785 --> 00:01:33.786
over a thousand pounds combined.

00:01:33.786 --> 00:01:35.553
As my release date got closer,

00:01:35.553 --> 00:01:37.618
I got into an altercation with an officer

00:01:37.618 --> 00:01:40.533
and was placed in solitary confinement.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.705
I was beaten and thrown into a cell.

00:01:42.705 --> 00:01:46.525
Alone with my thoughts,
I kept asking myself why.

00:01:46.525 --> 00:01:48.617
I wrote a 10 page letter out to my family

00:01:48.617 --> 00:01:50.349
explaining what happened

00:01:50.349 --> 00:01:53.273
and that I wasn't coming
home any time soon.

00:01:53.273 --> 00:01:55.900
And then I realized that I
didn't have a stamp to send it.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:59.099
After two weeks in solitary,
my sister sent me a letter

00:01:59.099 --> 00:02:02.100
and suggested I read
Psalm 91 from the Bible.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.070
I flipped open right to Psalm 91,

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:05.709
and that's when a stamp fell out.

00:02:05.709 --> 00:02:08.508
It was the stamp that I needed
to send out my letter with.

00:02:08.508 --> 00:02:10.557
I read the whole Bible from cover to cover

00:02:10.557 --> 00:02:12.908
and received a sense of peace and calm,

00:02:12.908 --> 00:02:14.432
despite my surroundings.

00:02:14.432 --> 00:02:16.528
My whole perspective on life changed.

00:02:16.528 --> 00:02:19.362
I began to believe that my
purpose was to give back

00:02:19.362 --> 00:02:21.869
instead of destroying
the people around me.

00:02:21.869 --> 00:02:24.620
When I got out, I realized
that my way of giving back

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.591
was through the world of fitness

00:02:26.591 --> 00:02:28.559
and that's when I started ConBody.

00:02:28.559 --> 00:02:30.326
ConBody is a president style boot camp

00:02:30.326 --> 00:02:32.461
that hires formerly
incarcerated individuals

00:02:32.461 --> 00:02:33.821
to teach fitness classes

00:02:33.821 --> 00:02:36.862
based on the workout I
developed in my cell.

00:02:36.862 --> 00:02:38.220
In just two and a half years,

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.179
ConBody has gone from workouts in the park

00:02:41.179 --> 00:02:44.872
to studios in NYC with 12 employees,

00:02:44.872 --> 00:02:49.319
over 7,000 clients and
over 200 classes per week.

00:02:49.319 --> 00:02:50.467
My business has been featured

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:53.435
in over 100 international media outlets.

00:02:53.435 --> 00:02:55.689
Today I travel the
country visiting prisons,

00:02:55.689 --> 00:02:58.525
training inmates in hopes
of creating a pipeline

00:02:58.525 --> 00:03:01.233
of trainers for ConBody.

00:03:01.233 --> 00:03:04.768
Our mission is to create a
bridge between two communities,

00:03:04.768 --> 00:03:08.184
young professionals and formerly
incarcerated individuals.

00:03:08.184 --> 00:03:11.846
At ConBody, we view each
other as real human beings

00:03:11.846 --> 00:03:14.026
and seek to break down the stereotypes

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:18.095
that formerly incarcerated
individuals face.

00:03:18.095 --> 00:03:20.189
Whoever dwells in the
shelter of the most high,

00:03:20.189 --> 00:03:22.673
will rest in the shadow of the almighty.

00:03:22.673 --> 00:03:24.988
(dramatic music)

00:03:24.988 --> 00:03:26.917
Thanks for reading, Coss.

00:03:26.917 --> 00:03:29.750
(dramatic music)

